  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water resource management and women&apos;s empowerment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will provide water resources to improve the access to potable water for 5,834 women and 4,286 men in marginalised communities in five Dioceses in Sri Lanka, together with provide training in good hygiene practices to 1,274 women and 965 men. The project will also provide training to enhance the capacity of vulnerable women in those communities to manage the water resources, and it is estimated that participation in project activities will increase the opportunities and confidence in decision-making for 1,751 women. By bringing together women from different communities for collective actions, the project will also contribute to harmony and reconciliation between and within these communities.</narrative>
  </description>
